        "raw-wiktextract-data.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "65f1c4e6-ec38-3e64-b8ea-d79c6e182c92",
                "word": "speared",
                "pos": "adj",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "a199ffef-52f0-3855-a9fc-98ae4b7767f5",
                        "entry_id": "65f1c4e6-ec38-3e64-b8ea-d79c6e182c92",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Wielding a spear."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "not-comparable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "9a0360db-4853-44e5-95f4-1d0ed6e1fdf2",
                                "sense_id": "a199ffef-52f0-3855-a9fc-98ae4b7767f5",
                                "text": "I must add, that a speared horseman, who said he had been sent to kill us, demanded ransom. The soldier coming up mediated. We compromised and the man got his fee. Perhaps, having a horse and spear, he was doing a job on his own account: if not, he got double pay."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "6ac12b75-0cb5-4c55-ac6f-f2a0bb0cfab7",
                                "sense_id": "a199ffef-52f0-3855-a9fc-98ae4b7767f5",
                                "text": "Taken any way one can, an army on paper is not a satisfactory profession. […] those who shape its destinies are so ready to direct it against matchlock monarchs and speared soldiery; […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "b536185d-b032-44c7-bee6-0ce03b404256",
                                "sense_id": "a199ffef-52f0-3855-a9fc-98ae4b7767f5",
                                "text": "The curtain on the third act was about to go up when we went back, and we were very surprised, as we stood there and gawked, to see a handful of gigantic hillbillies in overalls, red kerchiefs and straw hats mixed in casually with the gypsies, booted soldiers and speared warriors who were about to stride on."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
